(* Re < 2000: Martin extrapolated below its validity; treat as an optimistic bound.)

Literature check (same correlations, water-like Pr 4, nu 0.6e-6): a 0.1 mm nozzle at Ar 0.02 needs Re ~3000 (Vj ~18 m/s, jet dP ~250 kPa, j ~0.36 m/s = 14x our 2.56 cm/s) to reach ~250 kW/m2K. The 100-300 kW/m2K microjet results (Browne/Peles, Brunschwiler/IBM 31-126 um) live at 10-40x our volumetric flux density and 5-50x our dP.

## B. Slot-jet-into-micro-fin cell (uniform 128 W/cm2, j = 2.56 cm/s at 18 LPM)

h_eff = (h_fin 2H eta + h_base b)/p with region weighting: jet column + turn (x1 = w_n/2 + 0.5 H: descent flow at (Vj+u_ch)/2 on the fin walls, plane stagnation on the floor) and channel flow (entrance restarted). 'open-slot ref' = same fins and flow length fed like an HMMC (no jet). Core dP excludes ports/manifold.

