### C3. Equal pumping power and equal dP comparisons (15 kW, PCM)

- at HMMC-R hydraulic power at 18 LPM (1.8 W): JH-R runs 18.5 LPM -> 26.6 / 29.6 K (5.8 kPa); HMMC-R runs 18.3 LPM -> 27.9 / 30.9 K (5.9 kPa).
- at CoolIT-like at 18 LPM (6.5 W): JH-R runs 28.5 LPM -> 23.2 / 26.2 K (13.7 kPa); HMMC-R runs 28.2 LPM -> 24.8 / 27.8 K (13.8 kPa).

## D. Real 2027-28 package: 4 x 26 x 33 mm dies at 350 W/cm2 + 16 HBM at 40 W/cm2 (12.85 kW, 15.4 LPM)

Heat-proportional zoning (die block 91 % of flow, j_die = 3.0 x 2.19 = 6.6 cm/s), base 1.0 mm. Hottest-die case-to-inlet = caloric 6.7 + base 9.0 + TIM + q/h_eff_die (the nonuniform-heatmap fit dT = 33 + 3500/h_eff + 350(R_TIM - 0.05) reproduces HMMC-R 60.5/48.3 K). Nozzle zoning: equal nozzle dP in all zones, so die-zone jets run at the same velocity with ~3x the nozzle open area (shorter row pitch), HBM zone uses sparse 0.5 mm round orifices at the same dP.

