At 1.2 LPM/kW a 2-4 kW plate has 4-10x less flow per unit area than the 15 kW TTV; the jet velocity collapses (0.1-0.3 m/s at the same nozzle geometry) and the hybrid degenerates to a slot-fed manifold plate. Re-zoned (all nozzle area over the dies, see D) is where the GPU-class plate gets its jet benefit.

Die-concentrated GPU plate check (Rubin-class 2.3 kW, 2 reticle dies 16.5 cm2 carrying ~2.0 kW = 121 W/cm2, 90 % of 2.76 LPM over the 17 cm2 die block):
  - JH-R: j_die 2.4 cm/s, Vj 0.61 m/s, h_eff 153 kW/m2K; die case-to-inlet ~25.6 K (PCM) / 20.8 K (LM); core dP 0.3 kPa
  - open-slot ref: j_die 2.4 cm/s, Vj 0.61 m/s, h_eff 127 kW/m2K; die case-to-inlet ~27.2 K (PCM) / 22.4 K (LM); core dP 0.3 kPa

